# Code owners
#
# Every path that changes a contract, a money path, or a process needs a review
# from someone who owns it. GitHub requests a review from these owners
# automatically when a PR touches a matching path.
#
# NOTE: these are individuals, not teams. Teams do not exist yet. When a team is
# created, replace the handle here — GitHub silently ignores an owner it cannot
# resolve, so a typo in this file disables the review requirement without any
# visible error. Verify after every change to this file by opening a throwaway
# PR and confirming the reviewer is requested.

# Default: the money path and the contracts below get the most scrutiny.
# Last match wins, so the specific paths below override this.
*                       @BerlinDeskMudit

# Process and governance. Changing how people contribute needs maintainer sign-off.
# This covers .github/CONTRIBUTING.md, .github/SECURITY.md and
# .github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, which GitHub reads from this directory.
.github/               @BerlinDeskMudit

# Design decisions and the schema. An ADR or schema change invalidates downstream
# work, so it is reviewed before it lands rather than after.
/docs/adr/             @BerlinDeskMudit
/docs/architecture/    @BerlinDeskMudit

# Continuous integration. A weakened gate is a silent regression.
/.github/workflows/    @BerlinDeskMudit
